Draw the frame an input event dirtied inside the event; present with the transaction

This change applies to crates/gpui_macos/src/window.rs of
zed-industries/zed 90d8514059561f0e44af0a32e84e1c329cef3232
after 0001.

What it does:
- The frame an input event dirties is drawn inside that event, at most once
  per 3 ms, and a display-link tick within 8 ms of such a frame does nothing.
  The trackpad reports at 125 Hz against a 120 Hz display; drawing only at
  the tick alternated ticks carrying zero and two scroll events.
- A bounds-change (`displayLayer:`) frame stamps `last_input_frame` so the
  input event that follows does not draw a second frame.
- The display link's tick returns immediately during a live resize.
- Every frame presents with the transaction (the renderer's flag is never
  turned back off), and CATransaction is flushed at the end of every frame,
  so a hosted AppKit view's new frame and the scene it sits on reach the
  screen together.

Applied cleanly onto 90d8514 after 0001. #64958's frame journal stays:
each callback this patch draws passes RequestFrameOptions { signal_at,
signal_source } instead of Default::default(). displayLayer and the
key-status frame capture PlatformFrameSignal at entry; the display-link
frame drains WindowFrameSource::take_signal. rustfmt (1.98.1, edition
2024) makes no further changes.

Re-apply on a roll: git apply --3way patches/0002-frames-with-input.patch
